OpenBSD 7.9 VM automation

Automates install and first-boot setup of OpenBSD 7.9 in QEMU/KVM on a
Linux host, driven over serial (no VNC/OCR).

How it works

  vm.pl runs an install of OpenBSD 7.9 from the provided install media
  onto a raw disk image, answers the installer over the serial console,
  configures an encrypted softraid, boots the installed system through
  the UEFI loader, and performs post-install setup over SSH.

  Serial is on port 1234, the QEMU monitor on 1233.

Commands

  perl vm.pl all        full pipeline: install, boot, ssh setup, extras
  perl vm.pl boot       boot the installed system and wait for ssh
  perl vm.pl setup      post-install ssh/config setup
  perl vm.pl mnt        mount the guest disk from the host
  perl vm.pl halt       stop the VM

Prerequisites (host)

  - QEMU/KVM
  - OVMF firmware (OVMF.fd)
  - install image install79.img
  - vmkey SSH keypair; public key is injected into authorized_keys

Notes

  - The loader occasionally stalls reading the softraid volume; vm.pl
    retries with a monitor-issued reset.